  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An electron is orbiting an alpha-particle in a circular orbit with speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>. The mass of the electron is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> and the unified atomic mass unit is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"u\"></span>. What is the orbital radius of the electron?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{ke^{2}}{mv^{2}}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2ke^{2}}{mv^{2}}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{ke^{2}}{2uv^{2}}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{ke^{2}}{4uv^{2}}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
